<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Miramar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Laguna Miramar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Miramar is a lake in the Lacandon Forest of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiapas">Chiapas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. In the 16th century its island town of Lacam Tun was the stronghold of the Ch'ol-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lacandon-maya">Lacandon Maya</a>, who raided Spanish-held areas until an expedition destroyed it in 1586. It is now a protected area known for its clear waters and surrounding rainforest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-miramar.jpg" alt="Lake Miramar" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oleg Bozhenko aka MrGALL · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(21)_Miramar_Reservoir.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
